# The file must start with dwf-0.0 in order to be recognized.
# The rest of the first line is a comment.

# The file is divided into two sections, the first section contains
# general information about the weather data, the second the actual
# weather data. The general information have form of keyword: value
# pairs, which can be listed in any sequence.  All lines starting with
# `#' are also comments.  Empty lines are ignored

# General information about the station itself.

Station: Taastrup
Elevation: 30 m
Longitude: 12 dgEast
Latitude: 56 dgNorth
TimeZone: 15 dgEast

# Information about the measurement conditions.

Surface: reference
ScreenHeight: 2.0 m

# General information about the available data.

Begin: 1962-04-01
End:   2008-10-31
Timestep: 24 hours

Note: These data are only for test purposes.
Note: There is only a single logical note, but it can span multiple
Note: lines, all starting with `Note:'.

Note: Aggregated hourly precipitation used for period 1999-06-01 to 1999-06-20.
Note: Low quality aggregated hourly values used from 2001-10-8 to 2008-10-31.
Note: Precipitation from DMI Copenhagen used for 2002-06-02 to 2002-07-28.

# Fixed deposit values.

